From 9d493cf6e5d4636bef34e815adae37b0a9b40ef2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:40:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 59/69] CUDA/HIP: batch the small async input uploads of a
 graph into one H2D copy + one scatter launch (GGML_HIP_INPUT_BATCH)

A decode step uploaded its 12 graph inputs (LFM2: token embedding row, positions, KQ mask, K/V
cache row indices, recurrent state copy ids, the two 64x64 Hadamard inputs, out_ids, ...) as 12
hipMemcpyAsync calls before the graph launch: ~76 us on the GPU timeline under the profiler (32 us
of copy kernels plus the gaps), all on the critical path between two tokens.
set_tensor_async now copies non-empty uploads of up to 256 KiB into a pinned staging buffer (two
2 MiB halves, each reused after the event of its last H2D copy) and records the destinations; the
next other stream operation of the backend (graph compute - before any capture -, synchronize,
event record/wait, get/set 2d, get, tensor copies) flushes them as one H2D copy of the staging half
into a device staging buffer and one scatter kernel (8 KiB chunks per block). 316 -> 305 kernels per
LFM2 token; head of token t to first graph kernel of token t+1 under the profiler 168.7 -> 112.6 us
at depth 0, 162.7 -> 153.4 us at 98k (scatter 4.0 us there, the KQ mask is 192 KiB).

Bitwise (exact copies): logit hashes unchanged, greedy md5 LFM plain q8_0 (vec FA) 2c7ee8a2...,
Qwen plain c4708318..., Qwen MTP 6f14e814....
llama-bench tg128 -r 5, LFM2.5-24B-A2B, KV q8_0, interleaved: depth 0 (5 rounds) 3.840 -> 3.806
ms/token, depth 98304 (2 rounds) 5.230 -> 5.198 ms/token.
GGML_HIP_INPUT_BATCH=0: one hipMemcpyAsync per upload as before.
